{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3282","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3282","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3282\",\"parent_revision\":\"2aa18dbf337af751c8986d83277779961f533054c5dcdf13bd00b22fe4aff17c\",\"root_revision\":\"2aa18dbf337af751c8986d83277779961f533054c5dcdf13bd00b22fe4aff17c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDuring the grooming swarm for #3276, two teammates spawned via the `Agent` tool with subagent types that are supposed to be granted `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` (per their agent frontmatter `tools:` lists) reported they couldn't write their own sections:\\n\\n- `dh:impact-analyst` (spawned as `groom-3276-impact`): completed its full Impact Radius analysis, then reported \\\"I don't have `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` tools in this session (not granted / not connected), so I can't call `backlog_groom` myself,\\\" and pasted its finished section for the orchestrator to write on its behalf.\\n- `dh:fact-checker` (spawned as `groom-3276-factcheck`): completed its Fact-Check analysis, reported \\\"Ready to write findings to backlog item via `backlog_groom` MCP once server connects,\\\" then went idle without ever writing the section. The orchestrator had to detect the missing section (via `backlog_view`), send the idle agent a follow-up message, and only then did the write succeed.\\n\\nBoth are the same class of failure as #3276/#3248/#3250 (an agent's analysis silently fails to reach durable storage) but with a different specific cause: MCP tool grant/connection availability at spawn time, not a missing completion-report instruction. In both cases the underlying analysis work was fine \u2014 only the persistence step failed silently, requiring orchestrator intervention (writing on the agent's behalf, or nudging a retry) to avoid losing the work entirely. Not yet verified whether this is intermittent (a race between agent startup and MCP server connection) or reproducible on demand, or whether it affects other `dh:*` teammates spawned the same way in a grooming swarm (rtica-assessor, alignment-analyst, classifier, groomer all completed without this issue in the same #3276 session).\\n\\n**User-provided context**: possible directions for grooming to evaluate, not requirements \u2014 (1) determine whether this is a connection-timing race (agent starts working before its MCP server finishes connecting) that a startup wait/retry would fix, or a tool-grant configuration issue specific to how these two agent types get spawned in this workflow; (2) consider whether groom swarm agents should verify their own required MCP tools are available before beginning analysis, so a missing grant surfaces immediately rather than after the analysis work is already done.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-29, while grooming #3276 via /dh:work-backlog-item\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-28\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"58d1c9d3036fcb0dedde9cb80bca926928f739e1ded2698ac4cc86ba5d0021a2\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRSB3yA\"}"}